.TH SUMMARIZE_VIDEO 1 "October 11, 2026" "video-summarizer 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
summarize_video \- fetch a video's captions and summarize them with an AI model
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B summarize_video.py
.I URL
.RB [ \-\-model
.IR MODEL ]
.RB [ \-\-out
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-sections
.IR LIST ]
.RB [ \-\-provider
.IR auto | anthropic | openai ]
.RB [ \-\-base\-url
.IR URL ]
.RB [ \-\-price\-in
.I N
.BR \-\-price\-out
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-cookies\-from\-browser
.IR BROWSER ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-summary ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B summarize_video.py
reads the captions that already exist on a video, using
.BR yt\-dlp (1),
cleans them into timestamped text, sends them to a model, and saves
everything in one folder per video.
It does not transcribe audio, so a video with no captions fails with
an error.
.PP
Many users give the script a shell alias, such as
.BR vidsum ,
and call it that way.
.PP
.I URL
can be any address that
.B yt\-dlp
supports.
YouTube is the tested path.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-model " MODEL"
Model to use.
Default:
.B claude\-sonnet\-5
(or the value of
.BR VIDEO_SUMMARY_MODEL ).
Any other name is sent to an OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
.TP
.BI \-\-out " DIR"
Directory that holds the per-video folders.
Default:
.B ~/Documents/video\-summaries
(or the value of
.BR VIDEO_SUMMARY_DIR ).
.TP
.BI \-\-sections " LIST"
Comma-separated list of summary sections to request.
Valid names are
.BR tldr ,
.BR actionable ,
.BR key\-points ,
.BR walkthrough ,
and
.BR quotes ;
.B all
selects every section.
Sections always appear in that order, whatever order you type them in.
An unknown name stops the program before any download or model call.
Default:
.B tldr,actionable,key\-points,walkthrough
(or the value of
.BR VIDEO_SUMMARY_SECTIONS ).
See
.B SECTIONS
below.
.TP
.BI \-\-provider " auto" | anthropic | openai
Which provider path to use.
.B auto
(the default) picks Anthropic for
.B claude\-*
model names and the OpenAI-compatible path for everything else.
Setting
.B \-\-base\-url
or
.B OPENAI_BASE_URL
forces the OpenAI-compatible path.
.TP
.BI \-\-base\-url " URL"
An OpenAI-compatible endpoint, for example
.B https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
or
.B http://localhost:11434/v1
(Ollama).
.TP
.BI \-\-price\-in " N"
.TQ
.BI \-\-price\-out " N"
Dollars per 1,000,000 input and output tokens.
They set the cost estimate for models that are not in the built-in price table.
Give both; one alone is ignored.
.TP
.BI \-\-cookies\-from\-browser " BROWSER"
Send that browser's cookies to
.BR yt\-dlp ,
for example
.BR chrome .
Use this when YouTube answers with HTTP 429.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-summary
Fetch and format the transcript only.
No model call is made and no key is needed.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the program version and exit.
.SH SECTIONS
.TP
.B tldr
Two or three sentences on the whole video.
.TP
.B actionable
The part a viewer would act on, in the form that fits the video.
A list video gets a numbered list of every item.
A how-to gets prerequisites and numbered steps with the tools, settings and
amounts mentioned.
A ranking gets a list from best to worst with a reason for each.
Other videos get their specific conclusions or recommendations.
.TP
.B key\-points
The main points as bullets, in order.
.TP
.B walkthrough
The video split into its natural segments, each with a timestamp, a heading
and a short description.
.TP
.B quotes
Up to five short verbatim quotes with timestamps.
Off by default.
.SH OUTPUT
Each run creates a folder named
.IB DATE _ title-slug
inside the output directory, where
.I DATE
is the upload date.
The folder holds:
.TP
.B summary.md
The model's summary, with
.RB [ HH:MM:SS ]
markers.
.TP
.B transcript.md
Formatted transcript: chapters as headings, and paragraphs prefixed with
their start times.
.TP
.B transcript.txt
Plain transcript with a marker every 30 seconds.
This is the exact text sent to the model.
.TP
.B transcript.raw.vtt
The original subtitle file.
.TP
.B metadata.json
Video details, the tool version, the provider and model used, and the
sections requested.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
Key for the default Claude provider.
.TP
.B OPENAI_API_KEY
Key for OpenAI-compatible endpoints.
Local endpoints such as Ollama need none.
.TP
.B OPENAI_BASE_URL
Same effect as
.BR \-\-base\-url .
.TP
.B VIDEO_SUMMARY_MODEL
Default for
.BR \-\-model .
.TP
.B VIDEO_SUMMARY_DIR
Default for
.BR \-\-out .
.TP
.B VIDEO_SUMMARY_SECTIONS
Default for
.BR \-\-sections .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error, such as a missing
.BR yt\-dlp ,
a video with no captions, a download failure, an invalid
.B \-\-sections
value, or a model that declined to summarize.
.PP
If no API key is set, the transcript files are still saved, a warning is
printed, and the exit status is 0.
.SH EXAMPLES
Summarize a video with the default sections:
.PP
.RS
.nf
summarize_video.py "https://youtu.be/VIDEO_ID"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Only the list, steps or ranking:
.PP
.RS
.nf
summarize_video.py "https://youtu.be/VIDEO_ID" \-\-sections actionable
.fi
.RE
.PP
Add the quotes back:
.PP
.RS
.nf
summarize_video.py "https://youtu.be/VIDEO_ID" \-\-sections all
.fi
.RE
.PP
Make a section choice permanent:
.PP
.RS
.nf
export VIDEO_SUMMARY_SECTIONS=tldr,actionable
.fi
.RE
.PP
Retry after an HTTP 429 from YouTube:
.PP
.RS
.nf
summarize_video.py "https://youtu.be/VIDEO_ID" \-\-cookies\-from\-browser chrome
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use a local Ollama model:
.PP
.RS
.nf
summarize_video.py "https://youtu.be/VIDEO_ID" \-\-model llama3.1 \e
  \-\-base\-url http://localhost:11434/v1
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yt\-dlp (1),
.BR uv (1)
.SH AUTHORS
Project home: https://github.com/jboho/video-summarizer
